#  AI Job Hunter — configuration
#
#  Copy this file to `.env` in the same folder and fill in what you have:
#      cp .env.example .env          (macOS / Linux)
#      copy .env.example .env        (Windows)
#
#  ONLY ONE THING IS REQUIRED: an AI key. Every job board below is optional and
#  fails soft — a source with no key returns nothing and the run carries on with
#  whatever else is configured. The server prints which sources are live at boot.
#
#  Never commit `.env`. It is gitignored.


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  1. AI  — REQUIRED
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The app calls a model at three tiers: a cheap one that screens thousands of
# listings, a mid one that scores the survivors, and an expensive one that
# writes the verdicts you read. Roughly 100k tokens per run, ~90% of it on the
# cheap tier.
#
# Which PROVIDER is used is inferred from the MODEL NAME, per tier — so you can
# mix vendors. Anything containing "claude" goes to Anthropic, everything else
# to OpenAI.

OPENAI_API_KEY=
#   https://platform.openai.com/api-keys

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#   https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#   Only needed if you point a tier at a Claude model below.


# ── Which model runs at each tier ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  ⚠ THE DEFAULTS BELOW ARE OPENAI MODEL NAMES, and they are the specific ones
#    this pipeline's prompts were tuned against. If you are NOT using an OpenAI
#    key — or your OpenAI key cannot reach these particular models — you must
#    set ALL FOUR to models you can actually reach, or every run fails.
#
#    The failure is quiet, which is why this warning is here: a model call that
#    errors is caught by a deliberate fail-open path, so the search completes
#    and returns nothing useful rather than reporting an auth error.
#
#  The tiers differ in volume by orders of magnitude, so it is worth spending
#  differently on them: the cheap tier runs hundreds of times per search, the
#  judge one to three times.

ENGINE_CHEAP_MODEL=gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17
#   The screen gate. Highest volume by far — keep this one cheap.
ENGINE_MID_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
#   The 0-100 fit scorer.
ENGINE_EXP_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra
#   The final judge: reads full job descriptions and writes what you see on the
#   cards. 1-3 calls per run, so the best place to spend more.
ENGINE_EMBED_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
#   Embeddings for the semantic pre-filter. Vectors are cached forever per job,
#   so this is cheap after the first run.

# An all-Anthropic setup would be, for example:
#   ENGINE_CHEAP_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
#   ENGINE_MID_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
#   ENGINE_EXP_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# Anthropic has no embeddings API, so embeddings still need one of:
#   EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai   (default — keep an OpenAI key just for this), or
#   EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=voyage   (+ VOYAGE_API_KEY, https://www.voyageai.com)
# EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=
# VOYAGE_EMBED_MODEL=voyage-3.5-lite

# The lighter model tiers used for CV parsing (separate from the search pipeline
# on purpose, so tuning a search doesn't silently retune CV parsing):
# CHEAP_MODEL=gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17
# MID_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# STRONG_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra

# Any OpenAI-compatible server (OpenRouter, Groq, Together, LM Studio, Ollama).
# Set LLM_PROVIDER=openai as well if your model names don't look like OpenAI's.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
# LLM_PROVIDER=


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  2. JOB BOARDS — all optional, all free, listed most-useful first
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# With none of these you still get results: the ATS company boards (Greenhouse,
# Lever, Ashby, Workable, Recruitee, Personio, SmartRecruiters) need no key at
# all. But they are a narrow slice, so add at least one of the first two.

# ── Reed — the single biggest win for a UK search ──────────────────────────
#   https://www.reed.co.uk/developers/jobseeker  → sign up, key is instant
#   UK-only. The app also uses Reed's per-job endpoint to fetch FULL job
#   descriptions, which materially improves every downstream judgement.
REED_API_KEY=

# ── Adzuna — broad aggregator, 20+ countries ───────────────────────────────
#   https://developer.adzuna.com/  → register, both values on your dashboard
#   Free tier is generous. Needs BOTH values.
ADZUNA_APP_ID=
ADZUNA_APP_KEY=

# ── JSearch (via RapidAPI) — a Google-for-Jobs mirror ──────────────────────
#   https://rapidapi.com/letscrape-6bRBa3QguO5/api/jsearch  → subscribe to the
#   free tier, then copy the key from your RapidAPI dashboard.
RAPIDAPI_KEY=

# ── serper.dev — Google organic search ─────────────────────────────────────
#   https://serper.dev/  → 2,500 free queries on signup
#   Finds postings on company sites and smaller boards the aggregators miss.
#   This is the ACTIVE Google provider; SERPAPI_KEY below is the alternative.
SERPER_DEV_API_KEY=

# ── SerpAPI — alternative Google Jobs provider ─────────────────────────────
#   https://serpapi.com/  → 100 free searches/month
#   Only used when serper.dev is not configured.
SERPAPI_KEY=

# ── Careerjet — no key needed ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Works out of the box on a shared affiliate id. For anything beyond personal
#   use register your own at https://www.careerjet.com/partners/api
# CAREERJET_AFFID=
# CAREERJET_REFERER=http://localhost/

# ── USAJOBS — US federal roles only ────────────────────────────────────────
#   https://developer.usajobs.gov/APIRequest  → needs BOTH values; the
#   user-agent is the email address you registered with.
USAJOBS_API_KEY=
USAJOBS_USER_AGENT=


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  3. TUNING — cost vs. coverage. Defaults are tuned; all optional.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# See the README's "Tuning" table. The first one is the main cost dial.

# How many listings the CHEAP model examines per run. The single biggest lever
# on both cost and how deep the search goes. Lower it to spend less.
# RANK_EXAMINE_BUDGET=480

# How many survivors the mid tier aims to approve, and how many of those reach
# the expensive judge. JUDGE_POOL is the main driver of judge-tier spend.
# RANK_TARGET_POOL=80
# JUDGE_POOL=40

# Below this 0-100 mid-tier fit score a listing is dropped before the judge.
# RANK_REJECT_SCORE_FLOOR=32

# Max roles shown per run, and the per-role-family floor.
# FINAL_PICKS=12
# MIN_RESULTS=3

# Embedding cosine cutoff for entering the pool at all. Raise to search
# narrower and cheaper; the floor is clamped to never exceed the primary.
# RELEVANCE_PRIMARY=0.39
# RELEVANCE_FLOOR=0.39

# Hard ceiling on searches per day — your main protection against a surprising
# bill. A run costs roughly 100k tokens.
# MAX_SEARCHES_PER_DAY=6

# How many searches may run at once. Each drives its own headless Chromium, so
# this is really a memory ceiling.
# MAX_CONCURRENT_SEARCHES=2

# How many pages of results to pull per search term. More = deeper coverage,
# but it is paid in latency before the first cards appear.
# REED_PAGES_PER_TERM=3
# ADZUNA_PAGES_PER_TERM=3


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  4. SERVER — optional
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Where the frontend runs, for CORS. Add origins comma-separated.
# FRONTEND_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000

# SQLite by default, created automatically. Postgres works unchanged.
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./backend/jobmatch.db

# There is no login. If you expose this process beyond localhost, set this to
# require a header on the /admin maintenance endpoints — and put a real
# authenticating proxy in front of everything else.
# ADMIN_TOKEN=
